From 938aa0d92be1da4e9317e9a8babbf8ff23da1828 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: steamac <steamac@local>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 02:31:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] kk: keep compiled MSL libraries with the device

A title asks for the same MSL program once per pipeline: Dragon's Dogma 2
issues ~100 compile requests per distinct program in a single launch (87,243
library compiles for ~1,100 programs). Metal's own cache answers each request
in fractions of a millisecond, but every request still costs the round trip to
reach it (FEX -> vkd3d -> Venus -> virglrenderer -> this driver), milliseconds
each, and the same work is repeated for every pipeline.

Keep the compiled MTLLibrary by MSL source on the device instead: the library
is retained for the device's lifetime and returned from a hash table keyed by
the source string. On a warm Dragon's Dogma 2 launch this cuts library compiles
from 87,243 to 6,244, all compile requests from 131,636 to 34,051 and the total
Metal time from 80 s to 14 s (measured with MESA_KK_DEBUG=compiles).

Generated-by: LLM
